    {
      "id": "vepzl5u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Energy is a scalar quantity defined as the capacity of a body to do work, measured in Joules (J).",
        "Kinetic Energy (KE = ½mv²) is energy possessed by a body due to its motion.",
        "Potential Energy (PE = mgh) is energy stored in a body by virtue of its position, shape, or configuration.",
        "The Law of Conservation of Energy states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed, only transformed.",
        "Mechanical Energy is the sum total of Kinetic Energy and Potential Energy in a system.",
        "Power is the rate of doing work or transferring energy (P = W/t), measured in Watts (W)."
      ],
      "id": "wchooym"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y8464mf",
      "content": "• Energy is the capacity to do work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zhsxkbu",
      "content": "• Energy can exist in different forms such as mechanical energy, heat energy, electrical energy and chemical energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8453h2r",
      "content": "• The SI unit of energy is Joule (J)."
    },
    {
