    {
      "id": "uf92v8v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Law of Conservation of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "us2mzyx",
      "content": "The law of conservation of energy states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed; it can only be converted from one form to another."
    },
    {
      "id": "gvopkgj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Mechanical Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3gqyalc",
      "content": "Mechanical energy is the sum of kinetic energy and potential energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2dea27h",
      "content": "Mechanical Energy = KE + PE"
    },
    {
      "id": "zixab21",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Meaning of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bks4dar",
      "content": "Power is the rate at which work is done or energy is transferred."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c2pv8iq",
      "content": "Formula: Power = Work / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6740d1l",
      "content": "SI Unit of Power = Watt (W)"
    },
    {
      "id": "3zf4pya",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Units of Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "If the velocity of an object is doubled, its Kinetic Energy increases by 4 times (KE ∝ v²).",
